  <section id="callteam-ai" class="about-definition-section">
    <div class="container about-copy">
      <div class="section-label">CallTeam AI in simple English</div>
      <h2>AI prepares the account. Experienced people earn the conversation.</h2>
      <p><strong>CallTeam AI is the AI-assisted sales intelligence layer behind CallTeam's human-led B2B outbound work.</strong> It helps organize account research, decision-makers, buyer signals, campaign evidence, and call preparation before a person contacts the market.</p>
      <p><a href="/ai-lead-generation-services/">AI Lead Generation</a> finds, researches, and prioritizes potential accounts and contacts. The proprietary CallTeam Buyer Signal Radar identifies observable business changes worth investigating. <a href="/services/ai-gtm/">CallTeam AI GTM</a> connects that intelligence to campaign workflow, human calling, qualification, meeting handoff, and market learning.</p>
      <p>A signal is not proof that a company wants to buy. Experienced callers verify the situation, speak with the right people, qualify what is real, and book meetings only when there is a useful reason to continue.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-process-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">How the work moves</div>
      <h2>From intelligence to calling, qualification, and handoff.</h2>
      <div class="about-process-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Build the market view</h3><p>Define the ICP, buying problem, account criteria, decision-makers, proof, offer, and reason for a conversation.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Prepare the work</h3><p>Build or clean the list, research the account, review useful signals, prepare the call language, and define qualification.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Create the conversation</h3><p>Make the calls, listen, handle objections, follow up, qualify the opportunity, and protect the quality of the calendar.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Transfer and learn</h3><p>Book the next step, record useful context, update the CRM, support attendance, review outcomes, and improve the campaign.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-global-section">
    <div class="container-wide about-split">
      <div>
        <div class="section-label">Global B2B market coverage</div>
        <h2>International talent built around the market the client needs to reach.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy-stack">
        <p>CallTeam supports companies selling in the United States, Canada, across North America, and in global English-speaking B2B markets. We also help international companies build a practical route into the United States through clear market selection, relevant buyer language, real conversations, qualification, and market evidence.</p>
        <p>The CallTeam model brings together international sales talent with clear campaign standards. Geography does not replace judgment. Every campaign still needs the right account, the right person, a credible reason to talk, useful qualification, and a sales team prepared to handle the opportunity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

